[44.255115, "o", "  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/ 2>&1 | head -10\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ `ensurepip` thinks pip is already installed (because the dist-info is the…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify it works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip --"]
[44.255326, "o", "version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick sanity check — install a package to confirm it actually…\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 19 tool call(s) so far\r\nEverything is working now.\r\n\r\n**What was wrong:** The `pip` package files had been removed from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/`, but the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) was still present. This left pip in a broken state — the `pip3` executable existed and pointed to the right Python, but the actual `pip` module couldn't be imported.\r\n\r\n**What I did:**\r\n1. Removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory so `ensurepip` would recognize pip as missing.\r\n2. Ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade` to reinstall pip properly.\r\n3. Verified `pip3 --version` and a dry-run install both work.\r\n\r"]
